## Context
DESIGN-V2 §4 PR-9, honoring D3 in the contained scope the derivation critique
forced (M3): upstream's one global embedderId cannot support mixed spaces, so
the small PR is keep-vectors + pin the query-side embedder to the stored
vectorEmbedderId until a rebuild switches both. The verified violation dies:
dropStaleVectors -> clearVectors() at open silently zeroes semantic coverage
on any model change. Dual-embed migration stays in the RFC (0027). Failing
test: open a db under a different ZOTEUS_EMBEDDING_MODEL, watch semantic
coverage survive.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] vectors survive a model switch; query embedder pinned to stored id
- [ ] coverage/status names the pinned model
- [ ] PR opened upstream; outcome recorded here
